{
  "note": "Re-judged 2026-11-14 by an independent auditor who authored neither 08fe903803 nor the uncommitted phase 2 of spec-single-owner-lifecycle-2-bgp-session. RFC 2545 Section 3 read: \"A BGP speaker shall advertise to its peer in the Network Address of Next Hop field the global IPv6 address of the next hop, potentially followed by the link-local IPv6 address of the next hop.\" Units read: TestFamilyNextHopOriginationAdmission (both tags), TestDefaultOriginateAppendsLinkLocalWhenSection3Holds, TestDefaultOriginateRefusesUnusableIPv6NextHop (both tags), TestStaticGroupedResolvedNextHopWire, TestStaticOriginateContinuesAfterUnusablePolicyNextHop (both tags), TestStaticOriginateIPv6NextHopAdmission (both tags). 08fe903803 moved the initial-sync gate (sendingInitialRoutes) and the End-of-RIB owed mark (initialSyncEOROwed) from Peer onto Session. In the tagged units named stale it replaced peer.sendInitialRoutes() with peer.runInitialSyncNow(), which is Peer.sendInitialRoutes(p.testInitialSync()) (initial_sync_helpers_test.go): the same production sync body, run on the session the fixture installed (or one built with NewSession(p.settings) and published through establishedSession as enterEstablished does); it replaced peer.<flag>.Store(v) with peer.testInitialSync().<flag>.Store(v) or setTestInitialSync, and drainAndCloseQueueGate now takes that session. git diff 08fe903803^ against the working tree shows no assertion, expected byte, driven input or tag prose changed in any of them, each under the RFC-approved line 08fe903803 carries. Questions 1, 3 and 4 answer exactly as the earlier judgement below; question 2 still rests on the same producers, whose discrimination records are retaken by ./le rfc record after this stamp. Verdict unchanged: enforced. Earlier judgement follows. Re-judged 2026-11-03 by an independent auditor who authored none of 816ce1ce4c, 2cbd255ba4, 2e5c2d012a, d22b811ce4 or 1a2ccaeef8 (phase 5 of spec-filter-wire-0-umbrella, the per-peer text filter chain deleted). RFC 2545 Section 3 read: \"A BGP speaker shall advertise to its peer in the Network Address of Next Hop field the global IPv6 address of the next hop, potentially followed by the link-local IPv6 address of the next hop.\" Moved units TestFamilyNextHopForwardAdmission, TestRFC2545EffectivePairPolicyAndMixedSibling and TestStaticOriginateContinuesAfterUnusablePolicyNextHop changed only how the export filter answers: The test filter is now an answerTransport behind filterTransportSeam, compiled by answerPolicy into a policychain library chain, so the verdict travels the real filter-update path (route.Input, rpc.FilterUpdateOutput decoded by the library chain) instead of the deleted policyFilterSeam that handed a PolicyResponse straight to the text chain; that is the production path every plugin filter now takes. Each still answers the same raw replacement body (Modify with Raw) or accept, under the same conditions; in the pair test the per-family text match \"ipv6/unicast\" became a fields match on the IPv6 prefix, which the library chain sends once per UPDATE. Every expected byte is unchanged: exact MP_REACH value for valid fields, exact withdrawal for the loopback, invalid-first and invalid-second negatives, the legacy sibling kept with its own NEXT_HOP, and in the static test the refused first next hop still withdrawn while origination continues. A filter answer that the library path ignored would leave the raw-policy and valid-to-invalid rows announcing the received pair and fail them, and the \"policy never ran\" guards stay, so the polarity pair still discriminates. Ran the tagged units under ./le job run at HEAD (-tags ze_bgp, -v): PASS (scratch audit-p5-units-v.log). Verdict unchanged: enforced.",
